@zarpyk/dsh-mcp-manager README · Chat command：The outcome renders in the conversation and never enters the model's context. Aliases: `ls`, `enable`,
`disable`, `probe`, `reload`. Only the plugin's own pool can be exposed — discovered servers stay read-only until you
copy them into the pool.

@zarpyk/dsh-mcp-manager README · Files and storage：- State (pool + trash + last probe results): `$DSH_HOME/mcp-manager/state.json`
  (`%USERPROFILE%\.dsh\mcp-manager\state.json` on Windows by default).
- The file is written atomically (temporary file + rename) and is only touched by explicit actions.

@zarpyk/dsh-mcp-manager README · HTTP surface：Actions: `refresh`, `probe`, `spec`, `save`, `set-enabled`, `set-expose`, `delete`, `restore`, `purge`,
`empty-trash`, `import`, `export`.

Responses are `{ "ok": true, "data": … }` or `{ "ok": false, "error": "…", "code": "…" }`.
